{"type":"standard","title":"Rebecca Cooke (politician)","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Rebecca Cooke (politician)</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q139997274","titles":{"canonical":"Rebecca_Cooke_(politician)","normalized":"Rebecca Cooke (politician)","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Rebecca Cooke (politician)</span></span>"},"pageid":74526316,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Rebecca_Cooke_on_UpNorthNews_March_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Rebecca_Cooke_on_UpNorthNews_March_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":440},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/72/Rebecca_Cooke_on_UpNorthNews_March_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":774,"height":1032},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376309739","tid":"f913b73c-b73a-11f1-83a5-dc1f5bb7547c","timestamp":"2026-09-23T10:38:54Z","description":"American political candidate (born 1987)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebecca_Cooke_(politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebecca_Cooke_(politician)?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebecca_Cooke_(politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Rebecca_Cooke_(politician)"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebecca_Cooke_(politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Rebecca_Cooke_(politician)","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebecca_Cooke_(politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Rebecca_Cooke_(politician)"}},"extract":"Rebecca Cooke is an American nonprofit founder and former political consultant who is the Democratic nominee for Wisconsin's 3rd congressional district in the 2026 election. She unsuccessfully ran to represent the district in 2022 and 2024. From 2019 to 2021, Cooke served on the board of the Wisconsin Economic Development Corporation.","extract_html":"<p><b>Rebecca Cooke</b> is an American nonprofit founder and former political consultant who is the Democratic nominee for Wisconsin's 3rd congressional district in the 2026 election. She unsuccessfully ran to represent the district in 2022 and 2024. From 2019 to 2021, Cooke served on the board of the Wisconsin Economic Development Corporation.</p>"}